course: dictionary
lesson: 1044
title: Boredom and the mind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Boredom is the feeling you get when you have nothing interesting to do, or when you are not interested in what you are doing. «When you are bored with no screen, build a den, read, draw, write a story, do a puzzle or help cook.» Those are ideas for beating boredom.
explain: Boredom is a noun for a feeling, and it is uncountable. You cannot say "two boredoms", but you can say "a feeling of boredom" or "some boredom".
explain: Boredom is not always bad. «Boredom makes you notice things you would otherwise miss.» Some studies suggest boredom can lead to creative thinking because the mind starts to wander. A quiet, bored moment can lead to a new game or a story.
fact: Boredom means the feeling of being bored: having nothing interesting to do, or not being interested in what you are doing.
fact: Boredom is uncountable, so you do not say "a boredom" or "boredoms".
fact: «Out of boredom» means because you were bored. «Beat boredom» means stop feeling bored.
fact: A «boredom buster» is an activity that makes the bored feeling go away.
fact: Boredom is often the start of creativity: when your mind wanders, you may invent a game, draw a picture or write a story.
exercise: «Boredom makes you notice things you would otherwise miss.» What does boredom mean? | A kind of board game | Being tired after sport | *The feeling of having nothing interesting to do | A type of tasty food
exercise: Amit says, «I did the puzzle out of boredom.» Why did Amit do the puzzle? | Because he was asked by his teacher | Because he was very happy | *Because he had nothing interesting to do | Because it was his favourite game ever
exercise: Which phrase means getting rid of the feeling of being bored? | out of boredom | be bored by the sea | count boredom | *beat boredom
test: Which of these is a boredom buster? | A broken toy that nobody can use | A loud noise in the street | *Drawing a picture when you have nothing to do | A long, deep sleep at noon
test: Is boredom a word you can count? | No, because it is not a noun | *No, it is uncountable, so you say "some boredom" | Yes, but only in winter | Yes, you can say "two boredoms"
exam: «Some studies suggest boredom can lead to creative thinking.» What can boredom lead to? | *Creative thinking, because the mind starts to wander | Always feeling sad | Falling asleep at once | Being rude to friends
